/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 100 0 R
/T (This study aims to examine the differences in life expectancy across countries by analysing a range of economic, healthcare, educational, social, demographic, technological, and environmental indicators. The analysis begins with an assessment of the original dataset, followed by an investigation of the cleaned dataset to identify meaningful patterns and relationships. The primary objective is to determine the extent to which a country's economic wealth influences life expectancy and to explore the role of other factors that may contribute to differences in longevity.)
/E (This study aims to examine the differences in life expectancy across countries by analysing a range of economic, healthcare, educational, social, demographic, technological, and environmental indicators. The analysis begins with an assessment of the original dataset, followed by an investigation of the cleaned dataset to identify meaningful patterns and relationships. The primary objective is to determine the extent to which a country's economic wealth influences life expectancy and to explore the role of other factors that may contribute to differences in longevity.)
